meta {
  name: tag: docmost (stack)
  type: http
  seq: 23
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/docmost/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "stack",
    "stack_definition": {
      "restart_policy": "ordered",
      "secret_map": {
        "PG_PASSWORD": "${pods:random:32}",
        "APP_SECRET": "${pods:random:48}"
      },
      "members": [
        {
          "name": "db",
          "image": "postgres:16",
          "description": "Postgres 16 - Docmost stores all page/wiki content here (the critical durable store). local_only.",
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "networking": {
            "default": { "protocol": "local_only", "port": 5432, "tapis_auth": false }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "exec_command": ["pg_isready", "-U", "docmost", "-d", "docmost"],
              "initial_delay_seconds": 5,
              "period_seconds": 5
            },
            "networking_requires_ready": false
          },
          "environment_variables": {
            "POSTGRES_USER": "docmost",
            "POSTGRES_DB": "docmost",
            "POSTGRES_PASSWORD": "${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}",
            "PGDATA": "/var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata"
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 250, "cpu_limit": 2000, "mem_request": 256, "mem_limit": 2048 }
        },
        {
          "name": "redis",
          "image": "redis:7-alpine",
          "description": "Redis 7 - Docmost real-time collaboration / queues. local_only.",
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "networking": {
            "default": { "protocol": "local_only", "port": 6379, "tapis_auth": false }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "exec_command": ["redis-cli", "ping"],
              "initial_delay_seconds": 3,
              "period_seconds": 5
            },
            "networking_requires_ready": false
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 100, "cpu_limit": 1000, "mem_request": 128, "mem_limit": 1024 }
        },
        {
          "name": "docmost",
          "image": "docmost/docmost:latest",
          "description": "Docmost - open-source collaborative wiki/docs (own TipTap editor, real-time via Yjs). NOT an Office-file editor - no docx/pptx/xlsx, no slides.",
          "depends_on": ["db", "redis"],
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "environment_variables": {
            "APP_URL": "${:?Public URL Docmost is served at, e.g. https://mydocmost.pods.<base> - it bakes this into invite links}",
            "APP_SECRET": "${stack:secrets:APP_SECRET}",
            "DATABASE_URL": "postgresql://docmost:${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}@${stack:db:host}:5432/docmost?schema=public",
            "REDIS_URL": "redis://${stack:redis:host}:6379"
          },
          "networking": {
            "default": {
              "protocol": "http",
              "port": 3000,
              "tapis_auth": true,
              "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"],
              "tapis_auth_return_path": "/",
              "tapis_ui_uri_redirect": true,
              "tapis_ui_uri_description": "Docmost - first visit creates the admin account, then it's your wiki/docs workspace"
            }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "tcp_socket_port": 3000,
              "initial_delay_seconds": 15,
              "period_seconds": 10,
              "failure_threshold": 6
            }
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 500, "cpu_limit": 2000, "mem_request": 512, "mem_limit": 3072 },
          "compute_queue": "default"
        }
      ]
    },
    "tag": "latest-stack",
    "commit_message": "Docmost collaborative wiki/docs stack: docmost + postgres + redis. Own editor (TipTap/Yjs), env-driven, near-turnkey. Shared random PG password + APP_SECRET."
  }
}

docs {
  ## Docmost - the low-wizard "docs interface" (own UI, no OnlyOffice)

  Docmost is a self-hosted collaborative **wiki / knowledge base** (think Notion/Confluence). Unlike
  ONLYOFFICE Document Server, it ships its **own full frontend** - page tree, search, accounts,
  spaces, sharing - and its **own editor** (TipTap/ProseMirror + Yjs real-time). It does **not**
  embed OnlyOffice or Collabora.

  ### What it is / isn't
  - ✅ Collaborative rich-text pages, wikis, docs, comments, real-time co-editing, permissions.
  - ❌ **Not** an Office-file editor - no `.docx`/`.pptx`/`.xlsx`, **no slides, no spreadsheets**.
    If you need PowerPoint-style slides, that's the OnlyOffice/Collabora-engine path (heavier,
    wizardy), not Docmost.

  ### How many containers? Three.
  | member  | image                 | role |
  |---------|-----------------------|------|
  | db      | `postgres:16`         | **all page content lives here** - the store that must persist |
  | redis   | `redis:7-alpine`      | real-time collab / queues |
  | docmost | `docmost/docmost`     | the app + its own frontend, `depends_on` both |

  ### Why so little wizardry
  Everything is env-driven and resolves at instantiation:
  - `${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}` / `${stack:secrets:APP_SECRET}` - random, shared by reference.
  - `DATABASE_URL` / `REDIS_URL` - built from `${stack:db:host}` / `${stack:redis:host}`.
  - The only manual step is filling `APP_URL` (the public URL) and creating the admin account on
    first visit. No connector app, no admin-panel pasting, no replica-set init.

  ### Instantiate
  `POST /pods/stacks/from-template` with
  `{ "template": "docmost:latest-stack", "stack_id": "mydocmost",
     "pod_ids": { "docmost": "mydocmost" },
     "overrides": { "docmost": { "environment_variables": {
       "APP_URL": "https://mydocmost.pods.<base>" } } } }`
  -> open `mydocmost.pods.<base>`, create the first user, done.

  ### Persistence (recommended before real use)
  Both stores are on ephemeral pod disk here (frictionless first run). **Page content is in
  postgres** - that's the one to protect. Add a tapisvolume to the db member (prompts for a volume
  id at instantiation):
  ```json
  "volume_mounts": {
    "/var/lib/postgresql/data": { "type": "tapisvolume", "source_id": "${:?Tapis volume for Docmost postgres data}" }
  }
  ```
  File **attachments** (images/uploads) live on the docmost member at `/app/data/storage` - add a
  second tapisvolume there if you upload files you care about (or set `STORAGE_DRIVER=s3` + S3 env).

  > `tcp_socket` readiness on 3000 (connection-succeeds = up) is used instead of an HTTP path to
  > avoid pinning a health route. Pin `docmost/docmost:latest` to a concrete version for production.
}
